# canned-schedules Sphinx kit

Schedule admonitions for your Sphinx docs, styled like the Sphinx view of the canned-schedules preflight page:
tier colours from the configuration, a colour swatch per tier and Ubuntu fonts inside schedule
admonitions. Made for the [Furo](https://pradyunsg.me/furo/) theme, including its light, dark and auto modes.

Generated by canned-schedules {{ .version }} (config digest `{{ .digest }}`).

## Install

1. Copy the `_ext` folder next to your `conf.py`.
2. Add to `conf.py`:

   ```python
   import os, sys

   sys.path.append(os.path.abspath("_ext"))
   extensions += ["canned_schedules"]
   ```

3. Make sure `myst-parser` is installed (`pip install myst-parser`). The extension loads it and enables MyST's
   `colon_fence` extension, which the `:::` admonitions need.
4. Copy `examples/{{ .example }}` into your docs, or generate MyST for any request with
   `canned-schedules --myst-output-file schedule.md request.md`. Treat the MyST as build output: regenerate it from
   the requests in your docs build instead of editing it. The recipe is in the canned-schedules README, under "From
   request to docs page": <https://github.com/iilei/canned-schedules#from-request-to-docs-page>.

## What's inside

- `_ext/canned_schedules/__init__.py`: a local Sphinx extension. It adds the stylesheet and fonts to the build and
  enables `colon_fence`; nothing else.
- `_ext/canned_schedules/static/canned-schedules.css`: styles only schedule admonitions (`.admonition.schedule`, with
  `schedule-meta`, `schedule-base`, `schedule-tier` and `tier-N`). It sets Furo's admonition variables, so the theme
  keeps drawing everything; other admonitions and the rest of the site are untouched.
- `_ext/canned_schedules/static/fonts/`: Ubuntu and Ubuntu Mono (Ubuntu Font Licence, `UFL.txt`), used only inside
  schedule admonitions.
- `examples/{{ .example }}`: your request as MyST.

## Other themes

The colours, swatches and fonts work with any theme that renders admonitions as
`<div class="admonition …"><p class="admonition-title">`. Dark mode follows Furo's `data-theme` on `<body>`; other
themes show the light colours. The tier colours come from the configuration the kit was generated with: regenerate
the kit after changing it.
